@startuml 02-sequence-guided-web-form
title Guided Web Form — Ticket Creation (Sequence Diagram)

actor "Office Admin" as Admin
participant "Browser UI\n(public/app.js)" as UI
participant "HTTP Server\n(server/index.js)" as API
participant "Store\n(server/store.js)" as Store
participant "Triage Engine\n(server/triage.js)" as Triage
database "Site Register\n(server/data.js)" as Sites

Admin -> UI: Search house (address / name / phone)
UI -> API: GET /api/sites?q=...
API -> Store: listSites(query)
Store -> Sites: filter
Sites --> Store: matching sites
Store --> API: sites[]
API --> UI: 200 sites[]
UI --> Admin: Show matching houses

Admin -> UI: Select house
UI --> Admin: Show warranty / commissioning\n/ service-contract status

Admin -> UI: Fill fault type, error code,\nphotos, symptoms, safety checkboxes
Admin -> UI: Click "Create ticket"
UI -> API: POST /api/tickets {siteId, faultTypeId, ...}
API -> Store: createTicket(input)
Store -> Sites: getSite(siteId)
Sites --> Store: site record
Store -> Store: get prior tickets for site
Store -> Triage: triage(site, report, history)

alt gas smell or CO alarm flagged
  Triage --> Store: RULE_01/RULE_02\nemergency, P1, human callback
else commissioning date missing
  Triage --> Store: RULE_08\nback-office review
else
  Triage -> Triage: evaluate rule cascade\n(RULE_03..RULE_09)
  Triage --> Store: party, priority, chargeable,\nruleId, explanation
end
Triage --> Store: + repeat-fault flag,\n+ evidence completeness

Store -> Store: persist ticket to\ndata/tickets.json
Store --> API: ticket
API --> UI: 201 {ticket}
UI --> Admin: Show assigned party, priority,\nchargeable status, explanation

@enduml
